# US-112932 — [3a] Edit & Balance: Complete Button & History Queue — High-Level Analysis

## What Is Already True in the Database
Manual TAR jobs get a real row in `lat_TaxAmount_Summary` (`RunType='Manual'`, populated by
`sp_TaxAmt_Manual_Summary_iu`) — the exact same shared tracking table Mass jobs use, with the
exact same `isComplete`/`isHistory`/`CompletedDate`/`CompletedBy`/`isPayThruLereta`/
`ChecksRequired`/`RemitType`/`StatusDesc` columns already in place. This means:
- **No new column is needed** — `lat_TaxAmount_Summary.isHistory` already exists, shared with
  Mass jobs.
- **`Usp_Complete_EditBalanceJob` (the existing Mass-job Complete SP) may be largely reusable**
  for Manual jobs, rather than needing a brand-new SP from scratch — it already operates
  generically on `lat_TaxAmount_Summary`/`lat_TaxAmount_CheckData` by RunName/RunDate/CustID/
  AgencyID, with no Mass-only filter. What it still needs first is *some* check-data entry
  mechanism for Manual jobs (see "Open Dependency" below).
- **The existing 5-day History-queue job (`job_TaxAmount_MoveToHistoryQueue_u`) is NOT
  automatically safe for Manual rows** — it has no `RunType` filter, so once a Manual job's
  `isComplete` is set to 1, this job would flip it to History after 5 days, not the confirmed
  15-day window. This needs a small guard added (exclude `RunType = 'Manual'`).
- **The ELD-based History-queue job (`job_TaxAmount_MoveToHistoryQueueByELD_u`) is naturally
  safe** — it `INNER JOIN`s `lat_RPT_TCS384`, which Manual jobs never have a row in, so it can
  never match a Manual row. No change needed there.
- **The History Export SP (`sp_TaxAmount_Reports_Summary_Export_Excel`) already includes Manual
  rows generically** (TranType-branched subqueries, HAVING clause admits Manual rows) — most of
  AC5/AC6 is already covered. One gap remains: its `@RunType` filter parameter doesn't recognize
  `'Manual'` (only matches `'Supp'`/`'Initial'` via `JobSupInd`), so filtering the export by Run
  Type = Manual silently returns nothing.
- **A related bug was found**, not part of this story but relevant: the TAR Summary grid's own
  `SupInd` column (`sp_TaxAmount_Reports_Summary`) still mislabels every Manual job as "Initial"
  — see "Related Finding" below.

## What
Add a working "Complete" action for Manual TAR jobs on the Edit & Balance page, and ensure
completed Manual jobs move into History after 15 days (not the 5/10-day windows Mass jobs use) —
achieved primarily by reusing existing Mass-job mechanisms (already-shared table columns,
likely the same Complete SP) plus small, targeted guards/additions rather than parallel
Manual-specific plumbing. Also fix the History Export's Run-Type filter so it recognizes Manual.

## Why
Manual jobs share `lat_TaxAmount_Summary` with Mass jobs now, but nothing yet sets
`isComplete`/`CompletedDate` for them (no Complete action exists), and nothing yet enforces the
15-day (vs 5/10-day) History window specifically for Manual rows.

## What We're Working With
- **`Usp_Complete_EditBalanceJob`** — generic, keyed by RunName/RunDate/CustID/AgencyID; not
  Mass-specific by design. Candidate for direct reuse, pending the check-data-entry dependency.
- **`job_TaxAmount_MoveToHistoryQueue_u`** (5-day, no TCS384 join) — needs a `RunType != 'Manual'`
  guard added so it stops short of touching Manual rows.
- **`job_TaxAmount_MoveToHistoryQueueByELD_u`** (10-day, INNER JOINs TCS384) — inherently safe,
  no change needed.
- **New 15-day step/SP** — still needed, added to the existing "LASTax TaxAmount History Queue"
  SQL Agent job, filtered to `RunType = 'Manual'` (per confirmed answer).
- **`sp_TaxAmount_Reports_Summary_Export_Excel`** — mostly already Manual-aware; needs a small
  fix to its `@RunType` dynamic-SQL filter branch only.

## Technical Approach
- **Complete button — one click per Manual job:** unchanged conclusion — a Manual `RunName`
  always maps to exactly one Agency, so Complete operates on the whole job in one action.
- **Complete validation:** same rule as Mass jobs — entered check amount must match total due.
  **This still requires a check-amount entry mechanism for Manual jobs that no story has yet
  defined** — unchanged, still the single biggest open dependency (see Section 18 of the
  Detailed doc).
- **Status wording:** use `'Edit/Balance Completed'` (with slash) — unchanged, matches
  `StatusDesc`'s existing vocabulary on the now-shared `lat_TaxAmount_Summary` table.
- **History transition:** no new column needed (unlike the original plan) — add a small guard
  to `job_TaxAmount_MoveToHistoryQueue_u` (exclude `RunType='Manual'`), and add one new step/SP
  (15-day, `RunType='Manual'` filter) to the existing "LASTax TaxAmount History Queue" job.
- **Email notification:** unchanged — completing a Manual job does NOT trigger
  `job_ManualTarJob_EMail` (confirmed).
- **History Export:** most of the work is already done by the other team's PR; this story only
  needs to add a `RunType = 'Manual'` branch to the `@RunType` filter parameter's dynamic-SQL
  logic in `sp_TaxAmount_Reports_Summary_Export_Excel`.

## Related Finding (flagged, needs your triage — shared with US-132325)
`sp_TaxAmount_Reports_Summary`'s `SupInd` output column was never updated to recognize the new
`RunType = 'Manual'` column — Manual jobs currently display as "Initial" on the TAR Summary grid,
silently breaking the already-shipped Run Type filter/alert (US-112929). Not part of this
story's original file list, but worth deciding who fixes it, since it may affect how reliably
this story's own Complete-button UI can detect "this is a Manual job" if it ever keys off
`SupInd` instead of `RunType` directly.

