## What Changes
- A Manual job on the Edit & Balance page can be marked "Complete" once its entered check amount
  matches the total due (mechanism for entering that amount still TBD).
- 15 days after completion, a Manual job automatically moves to History via a new step in the
  existing daily History Queue job, without disturbing the existing 5/10-day Mass-job jobs.
- The History Export's Run Type filter correctly includes Manual jobs when filtered.

## What Stays the Same
- Mass-job Complete/History-queue behavior is completely unchanged.
- No Mainframe/payment-file integration is added for Manual jobs.
- Completing a Manual job does not send any email notification.

## Expected Outcome
Manual TAR jobs gain a full Current → Completed → History lifecycle on the Edit & Balance page,
achieved with a small SQL footprint (no new column, likely reuse of the existing Complete SP),
while the check-amount entry mechanism for Manual jobs remains an explicitly flagged, still-open
dependency to resolve before implementation.

